MinGW on msvcrt: timespec_get / TIME_UTC for SPU_INTERP_STATS (spu_interp.c) and SPU_JOBPROF (spu_workload.c).

Symptom: ps3recomp v0.17.0 (a6d76c8) does not build for Killzone 2 (remote build): spu_interp.c:520
"implicit declaration of function 'timespec_get'" and "'TIME_UTC' undeclared" (upstream c08d1d8 moved
SPU_INTERP_STATS to timespec_get; spu_workload.c's SPU_JOBPROF uses it too). Cause: KZ2's MinGW-w64 gcc targets
msvcrt (__MSVCRT_VERSION__ 0x600, no _UCRT), whose <time.h> has no C11 timespec_get; the UCRT has it. Fix: a small
header, runtime/platform/mingw_timespec_get.h, included by both files after <time.h> (and after <windows.h> in
spu_workload.c): on msvcrt MinGW only, TIME_UTC and a timespec_get from QueryPerformanceCounter (monotonic, not UTC;
both callers only subtract two readings). Other toolchains are unchanged. Upstream candidate (general).
Verification: x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc -fsyntax-only on both files; the remote build of kz2.exe.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (hand-merged): both sides kept

diff --git a/runtime/platform/mingw_timespec_get.h b/runtime/platform/mingw_timespec_get.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1fa2c84
--- /dev/null
+++ b/runtime/platform/mingw_timespec_get.h
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+/* C11 timespec_get for MinGW-w64 on msvcrt. The UCRT has timespec_get and TIME_UTC; msvcrt.dll does not, and
+ * MinGW's <time.h> declares neither there, so SPU_INTERP_STATS (spu_interp.c) and SPU_JOBPROF (spu_workload.c) did
+ * not compile. Both only subtract two readings, so this returns QueryPerformanceCounter time (monotonic, not UTC).
+ * Include after <time.h> and, if the file uses it, after <windows.h>. */
+#ifndef PS3RECOMP_MINGW_TIMESPEC_GET_H
+#define PS3RECOMP_MINGW_TIMESPEC_GET_H
+#include <time.h>
+#if defined(__MINGW32__) && !defined(_UCRT) && !defined(TIME_UTC)
+#define TIME_UTC 1
+#ifdef _WINDOWS_   /* <windows.h> is in: use its prototypes */
+static inline long long ps3_tsg_counter(long long* freq)
+{
+    LARGE_INTEGER c, f; QueryPerformanceFrequency(&f); QueryPerformanceCounter(&c);
+    *freq = f.QuadPart; return c.QuadPart;
+}
+#else
+__declspec(dllimport) int __stdcall QueryPerformanceCounter(long long* c);
+__declspec(dllimport) int __stdcall QueryPerformanceFrequency(long long* f);
+static inline long long ps3_tsg_counter(long long* freq)
+{
+    long long c; QueryPerformanceFrequency(freq); QueryPerformanceCounter(&c); return c;
+}
+#endif
+static inline int ps3_timespec_get(struct timespec* ts, int base)
+{
+    long long f = 1, c = ps3_tsg_counter(&f);
+    if (f <= 0) f = 1;
+    ts->tv_sec = (time_t)(c / f);
+    ts->tv_nsec = (long)((c % f) * 1000000000LL / f);
+    return base;
+}
+#define timespec_get ps3_timespec_get
+#endif
+#endif
